# Orion-X Phoenix Edition v2.1.0
# Package list for live-build (Debian Bullseye)
#
# @decision DEC-PHASE9-004
# @title GUI networking stack: NetworkManager + nm-applet + firmware
# @status accepted
# @rationale rc3 had no GUI networking — the live user could not connect to
#   Wi-Fi via the desktop. Fix: add network-manager (daemon + CLI), network-
#   manager-gnome (nm-applet tray icon, ships /etc/xdg/autostart/nm-applet.desktop
#   so it starts with any XDG-compliant session), wpasupplicant (WPA2/WPA3
#   supplicant for Wi-Fi), iw (nl80211 wireless CLI), and non-free firmware
#   packages for the most common Wi-Fi chipsets (Intel iwlwifi, Realtek r8188eu/
#   rtl8xxxu, Atheros/QCA ath9k/ath10k, and misc-nonfree covering many others).
#   non-free is already enabled in iso/auto/config via --archive-areas
#   "main contrib non-free" — no additional apt source config is needed.
#   NM's own postinst enables NetworkManager.service; the 0615 hook does not
#   need to enable it separately (NM handles its own systemd integration).
#   nm-applet autostart: network-manager-gnome ships
#   /etc/xdg/autostart/nm-applet.desktop which live-build copies into the
#   image verbatim — no explicit staging required.
#
# Packages marked EXTERNAL are NOT in the standard Debian Bullseye repos.
# They must be installed via separate mechanisms (custom .deb, pip, or
# third-party repo) and are commented out here so apt does not fail the
# live-build.  See docs/DEVELOPMENT_CHECKLIST.md for install procedures.
#
# W11-2 debloat pass (DEC-PHASE11-003 + DEC-PHASE11-006):
#   Removed: hashcat, john, hydra, proxychains, chntpw, steghide, encfs,
#            openvpn, build-essential, gcc, make, libssl-dev, python3-dev, vim
#   Retained: aircrack-ng, neovim, screen, tmux
#   Dev toolchain (build-essential, gcc, make, python3-dev, libssl-dev) deferred
#   to W11-8 optional installer (install-devel.sh). Operators who need a
#   build environment post-boot use the optional installer.
#   Offensive kit residue removed from base ISO mission-fit profile.

# Base system
live-boot
live-config
live-tools
dbus
eject
locales
sudo
user-setup

# Desktop environment
xfce4
xfce4-terminal
lightdm

# Forensic tools
# EXTERNAL: autopsy          — install via https://www.autopsy.com/download/
binwalk
# EXTERNAL: bulk-extractor — not in Bullseye main; available in contrib or
# via separate install. Disabled to unblock live-build. Tracked: jarocki/orion#33
# bulk-extractor
dc3dd
foremost
# EXTERNAL: ghidra           — deferred to W11-8 optional installer (install-ghidra.sh)
#                              per DEC-PHASE11-004. Run: /opt/orionx/optional/install-ghidra.sh
hexedit
sleuthkit
tcpdump
testdisk
# EXTERNAL: volatility3      — install via: pip3 install volatility3
wireshark
# EXTERNAL: zeek             — install via https://zeek.org/get-zeek/

# GUI Networking (rc4: Wi-Fi and wired connectivity via NetworkManager)
# NM daemon + CLI; postinst enables NetworkManager.service automatically.
network-manager
# nm-applet tray icon; ships /etc/xdg/autostart/nm-applet.desktop for
# automatic startup in XFCE and any other XDG-compliant desktop session.
network-manager-gnome
# WPA2/WPA3 supplicant (Debian package name is wpasupplicant, not wpa_supplicant)
wpasupplicant
# nl80211 wireless configuration CLI (iw, not wireless-tools/iwconfig)
iw
# Non-free Wi-Fi firmware for common chipsets:
#   firmware-iwlwifi   — Intel Wireless (iwlwifi driver, most Intel laptops)
#   firmware-realtek   — Realtek Wi-Fi (r8188eu, rtl8xxxu, rtw88, etc.)
#   firmware-atheros   — Atheros/QCA (ath9k, ath10k)
#   firmware-misc-nonfree — Broadcom, MediaTek, and many other chipsets
# These require --archive-areas "main contrib non-free" in iso/auto/config
# (already set, see DEC-PHASE9-004).
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-misc-nonfree

# Networking tools
curl
dnsutils
ethtool
fping
iputils-ping
netcat-openbsd
nmap
smbclient
ssh
traceroute
wget
wireguard-tools

# Security tools
apparmor
apparmor-utils
apparmor-profiles
apparmor-profiles-extra
aircrack-ng
clamav
cryptsetup
# fail2ban — SSH brute-force defense; modernized replacement for the obsolete
# denyhosts concept in gecko/bin/start-denyhosts.sh. The package postinst
# enables fail2ban-server.service via dh_installsystemd (same pattern as
# network-manager in W9-1 DEC-PHASE9-004 — no custom systemd unit needed).
# @decision DEC-PHASE9-018
# @title fail2ban replaces gecko/bin/start-denyhosts.sh
# @status accepted
# @rationale denyhosts is unmaintained and not in Debian Bullseye. fail2ban
#   provides equivalent SSH brute-force defense with active Debian packaging
#   and systemd integration. Daemon is enabled by the package's own postinst
#   (dh_installsystemd); no custom hook or unit file required (same as NM).
fail2ban
lynis
macchanger
nftables
# EXTERNAL: nikto — not in Bullseye stable repos; available in backports.
# Disabled to unblock live-build. Tracked: jarocki/orion#33
# nikto
rkhunter

